# RevHarness Critical Invariants (Cursor)

This rule is **always applied** to every Cursor agent session in this
repository. It encodes fail-closed RevHarness invariants. Detailed
operational guidance lives in `revharness-detailed.mdc` (description-
based attach).

## No raw secrets in output

Do not print tokens, keys, credentials, PII, or raw sensitive payloads.
Examples include `AKIA*`, `ghp_*`, `sk-*`, and
`-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----`.
When a detected value must be referenced, use redacted preview format:
`<prefix4>...<suffix4> (len=N)`.
Treat any violation as a RevHarness security boundary failure.

## No outbound cross-family wrapper invocation

Cursor agents in this session must not invoke `scripts/codex-wrapper.sh`
or `scripts/claude-wrapper.sh`.
Delegation to another agent family is owned by the orchestrator
(Claude or Codex top-level), not by Cursor.
When shell execution would reference either wrapper path, refuse it.

## `--mode ask` invocation = strict read-only

When invoked with `--mode ask`, do not write files or run shell commands.
If an operation needs file changes, respond exactly:
`this requires --mode agent or --role agent — please re-invoke`.
Tracked and untracked file modifications are forbidden in ask mode.

## Truth matrix is acceptance authority

`docs/manual/verification-truth-matrix.md` is the source of truth for
acceptance, LGTM, and completion.
Do not declare completion from wrapper success or rule guidance alone.
Completion requires execution evidence for the required deterministic
checks named by the applicable slice or matrix.

## `.shared/project_id` is immutable

Do not modify, delete, rename, normalize, or regenerate
`.shared/project_id`.
Keep this identity artifact stable for the full project lifecycle.
If it is missing or malformed, fail closed and report the blocker.
